.TH "YAMLR-FIX" "1" "November 2026" "Yamlr Manual" "User Commands"
\fBInstant Zero-Configuration Auto-Repair\fR
.PP
The \fBfix\fR command is the zero-configuration auto-repair pathway for Kubernetes manifests, applying safe, non-destructive schema upgrades, deprecation migrations, and syntax fixes without requiring complex flags.
.PP
.SH "USAGE"
.nf
.RS
yamlr fix [PATH]... [FLAGS]
.RE
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Equivalent to running \fByamlr heal --apply\fR with conservative, deterministic defaults:
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **Deprecation Upgrades**: Automatically transitions deprecated API groups to current stable versions (e.g. \fBextensions/v1beta1\fR -> \fBapps/v1\fR, \fBpolicy/v1beta1\fR -> \fBpolicy/v1\fR).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **Floating Tag Pinning**: Detects dangerous \fB:latest\fR floating container tags and converts them to pinned references.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **Zero-Comment Loss**: AST token-level rewrites ensure developer comments, Helm template blocks, and annotations remain 100% intact.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  **Atomic Invariant Rollback**: Verifies the mutated document before writing to disk; rolls back immediately if any syntax invariant is violated.
.SH "FLAGS"
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB-k, --k8s-version <VERSION>\fR: Target Kubernetes version (default: \fB1.30\fR).
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB--diff\fR: Display colorized inline word diff before applying mutations.
.IP "\(bu" 2
  \fB-h, --help\fR: Display help information for \fBfix\fR.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.nf
.RS
# Instantly heal all manifests in the current directory in-place
yamlr fix .

# Fix a specific deployment manifest
yamlr fix ./k8s/deployment.yaml
.RE
.fi
